  "manual": [
    "GET /auth/me/ uses request.user + MeSerializer(id,email,role): it must NOT be reported as BOLA or sensitive-field exposure.",
    "Views with no explicit permission_classes are covered by the global IsAuthenticated default: they must NOT be reported as 'no auth guard'. Explicit AllowAny/[] are only register, healthz (and token/docs/webhook).",
    "DELETE /patients/{id}/ is admin-only; PatientListSerializer hides ssn (list is safe, retrieve/create expose it) — check the nuance is right.",
    "v2 appointments are properly scoped (admin/doctor/creator) and cancel uses get_object(): v2 must NOT be reported as BOLA; v1 must be.",
    "Invoice.pay compares the client amount with invoice.total: it must NOT be reported as 'client-trusted payment amount' (it may note no gateway call).",
    "NotificationListView filters by request.user: it must NOT be reported as BOLA.",
    "notifications/consumers.py is a real websocket consumer (not a stub); notifications/worker_utils.py is a pure helper (not messaging); Celery worker is started via Procfile (must NOT be called an unwired orphan).",
    "Upload: Django sanitizes upload.name; the real traversal risk is request.data['filename']. The report must put the risk on the filename parameter, not claim upload.name traversal.",
    "Split analysis (>30 files): endpoint numbering/severity/commit hash are one continuous scheme; no endpoint duplicated or missing across app boundaries.",
    "Severity consistency (one flaw => one icon, summary 'critical N' counts only red) and no invented endpoints/flaws (e.g. Django admin, DefaultRouter api-root as a real feature)."
  ]
}
